From f7932d20a8d015984fbba935b8ee4027e8e5b82b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 02:47:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add AI lead qualification from WhatsApp conversations
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fills the previously-empty leads.ai_qual_score / ai_qual_profile /
ai_qual_at columns by scoring real WhatsApp conversations with Claude.

The feature operates on the CRM tables (whatsapp_messages + leads), not
the bot's own specto_bot_* tables — production conversations live in
whatsapp_messages (chat_id "<phone>@c.us", direction in/out) and leads
join by phone_norm (last 10 digits of the number) within a project_id.

- db.js: REST helpers getRecentWaChats / getLeadForPhone /
  getConversation / saveQualification (raw fetch, Node 18 friendly).
- handlers/qualify.js: builds a transcript, forces a structured result
  from Claude via a tool schema (score 0-100 + budget/urgency/niche/
  readiness/summary/signals), writes it to the lead. Orchestrator
  supports dry-run, per-chat targeting and re-qualification.
- index.js: optional poller, OFF by default behind QUAL_ENABLED. Scans
  recent chats each interval and qualifies not-yet-scored leads.
- scripts/qualify.js: CLI for backfill and safe --dry-run testing.
- tests for the pure logic (phone/transcript/parse/clamp).

Poller stays disabled until explicitly enabled in the deploy env.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WhWkrr6qa6rRytE2dZhGqE
