From 1e9aa102d5bc1644eb75c36fd5f3e7c08d67156b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 14:20:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add self-healing watchdog for lead qualification
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Strengthens the qualification subsystem so transient errors stop turning
into permanent gaps. Four reinforcements, all behind WATCHDOG_ENABLED
(off by default):

- Reliability: db.js gains withRetry (exponential backoff) wrapped around
  every Supabase request (GET/PATCH only — POST inserts are not retried to
  avoid duplicates) and around the Claude qualify call. Fewer spurious
  ai_failed and DB blips.
- Auto-heal: handlers/watchdog.js re-runs qualification over the whole
  history each cycle, picking up leads the poller missed or that failed
  transiently (reason=missing), and re-qualifying conversations that got
  new messages after scoring (reason=stale).
- Quality self-check: isSuspicious() flags inconsistent scores (hot but
  low / cold but high / empty summary / high score with unknown niche);
  the watchdog re-qualifies those (reason=qc).
- Monitoring + alerts: healthPing() checks Supabase, plus API-key presence;
  sendAlert() posts to WATCHDOG_ALERT_WEBHOOK (or logs) on DB down, missing
  key, or qualification failures.

index.js runs the watchdog on a slow interval (default 1h) behind its own
flag. New tests cover withRetry, isSuspicious and the summary reducer
(23 tests pass).
